# tierd secrets — example. Copy to `tierd.env` (systemd) or use with
# `docker compose --env-file` (Compose) and fill in real values.
#
# NEVER commit the filled-in file. Keep it mode 0640 (systemd: owned root:tier)
# or 0600. Secrets belong in the environment or in an @/path/to/file referenced
# by the flag — never as a literal flag value (those leak via ps / shell history).
#
# Generate a token or secret with:  openssl rand -hex 32

# Write/admin API token. REQUIRED for any non-loopback bind (fail-closed) —
# tierd refuses to start on 0.0.0.0 without it. Sent as `Authorization: Bearer`
# on writes and score GETs, and `X-Tier-Token` on the proxies.
TIER_API_TOKEN=

# Read-only viewer token (optional). A second bearer credential that grants only
# GET /scores, /scores/{developer}, and /metrics — hand this to a Prometheus
# scraper or a CFO/VP-Eng dashboard viewer. MUST differ from TIER_API_TOKEN
# (equal values are refused at startup). Alone it does NOT permit a non-loopback
# bind. Leave empty to disable the read scope.
TIER_READ_TOKEN=

# GitHub webhook HMAC secret (optional). Empty = POST /webhook/github is not
# mounted (fail-closed). Set it to the same secret configured on the GitHub
# webhook. See docs/webhook-setup.md.
TIER_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# Reporting mode (team|developer). REQUIRED with no default — tierd exits at
# startup if it is unset from every source. The systemd unit sets it in the
# config file and the Compose command sets it on the command line, so you
# normally do not need it here; uncomment to override those.
# TIER_AGGREGATION=team

# Alternative to putting a secret directly here: point the flag at a file.
#   tierd serve --api-token @/run/secrets/tier-api-token ...
# tierd reads the token from that file, keeping it out of the environment too.
